    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certifies that on 12th January 2006, the erection of a rear roof extension, with dimensions 5.4m wide x 4.3m deep x 2.1m high, which will increase the volume of the original house by 23.87 cubic metres, as shown on drawing numbers 5161, received 12/01/06, and drawings rear elevation and side elevation received 06/03/2006, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nFollowing the proposed extensions consisting of a rear roof extension, the resulting building would fall within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A and Class C, of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995.\r\n"
